{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 63, :comments ["<b>And Isaac went out to meditate.</b> He turned aside from the road in order to pour out his discourse before HaShem in the field, so that passersby would not interrupt him. Even though he had already prayed at <b>Be'er Lechai Ro'i</b>, and before he prayed he was answered — after the manner of (Daniel 10:12), \"From the day that you set your heart to humble yourself, your words were heard.\"" "<b>And behold, camels were coming.</b> And when he went out to meditate, his way was to meet them, as she said: <b>the one walking in the field to meet us</b>. This is because on his return from Be'er Lechai Ro'i to his home, his route was from north to south, and those coming from Haran to Abraham's house traveled from east to west. Therefore, when he turned aside from his route — which was from north to south — and walked eastward toward the path of the camels coming from the land of the children of the east, Rebekah supposed that he was walking to meet her."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:35.118812890Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}